# CODEOWNERS — audiomax.ai
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# THESE ARE REVIEW ROLES, NOT GITHUB ACCOUNTS.
#
# The names below are Studio Zero review agents, not usernames or teams. GitHub
# resolves an owner to a user, a team or an email address, and none of these
# resolve to any of those — so GitHub will not auto-assign from this file and
# will report the entries as invalid if branch protection is switched on with
# "require review from Code Owners".
#
# This file is therefore ADVISORY until real handles exist. It answers "who
# reviews a change here, and against which persona" — which is the question that
# actually gets asked, and which was previously answered only by reading
# CLAUDE.md and the roadmap side by side.
#
# TO MAKE IT ENFORCEABLE: replace each role with the `@handle` of the human or
# team that carries it, keeping the role name in the trailing comment so the
# reasoning survives the substitution.
#
# Personas live at C:\Users\Administrator\studio-zero\agents\<layer>\<name>.md
# and are invoked by spawning a subagent with the persona file as its system
# context. Reviewers get READ-ONLY tools — Jury Rule 4 is enforced by tool
# scope, not by instructions.
#
# AUTHORITY. CLAUDE.md owns the agent roster. The ROADMAP is the sole authority
# for which reviewer gates which PHASE — this file maps PATHS, which is a
# different question, and it must not be read as a phase assignment. Where a
# path and a phase disagree, the roadmap wins and this file is defective.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────


# ── Default ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Jury owns the commit gate for everything. No path is exempt.
*                               Jury            # audit/jury.md


# ── Governance and the review trail ──────────────────────────────────────────
/CLAUDE.md                      Jury            # the working agreement; owner-approved changes only
/resources/audits/              Jury            # verdicts and punch lists — committed, never rewritten
/.gitignore                     Vault  Jury     # security/vault.md — the audits exception and the secret rules
/.env.example                   Vault  Scribe   # the template whose whole job is to be safe to commit
/.github/scripts/               Vault  Forge    # secret-scan.mjs IS the key-material control
/.github/workflows/             Forge  Vault    # what actually runs the gates
/package.json                   Forge            # scripts here are the only invocation path for every gate
/eslint.config.mjs              Forge            # found by [WS-OWNED] on its first run, not by review
/supabase/tests/                Atlas  Probe    # quality/probe.md — the schema proofs


# ── Documentation (Scribe owns; Guide reports to Scribe) ─────────────────────
/README.md                      Scribe          # docs/scribe.md — mirrors, never originates
/CONTRIBUTING.md                Scribe
/CODEOWNERS                     Scribe
/docs/                          Scribe
/docs/architecture/             Scribe  Forge   # backend/forge.md co-signs architectural decisions
/docs/glossary.md               Scribe  Tongue  # platform/tongue.md — terms become catalogue strings
/docs/help/                     Guide  Proof    # docs/guide.md drafts; audit/proof.md grades before it ships
/docs/api/                      Nexus  Scribe   # backend/nexus.md owns the contract; Scribe owns the reference


# ── The documentation gate ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Weakening a check to make a document pass is the failure this tool exists to
# prevent, so a change here needs the reviewer who audits guard quality.
/tools/doc-check.mjs            Forge  Jury


# ── Backend services (planned — none of these paths exist yet) ───────────────
/worker/                        Forge           # backend/forge.md
/worker/src/queue/              Queue           # backend/queue.md — job queues and the render pipeline
/worker/src/providers/          Forge  Oracle   # ai/oracle.md — cost-per-interaction and eval
/worker/src/adapters/           Forge  Shield  Halo  # backend/forge.md writes it; security/shield.md (SSRF, archives) + audit/halo.md (extraction fidelity) review it
/worker/src/normalize/          Forge  Tongue  Halo  # backend/forge.md owns the TypeScript; platform/tongue.md the per-language rule sets and what gets spoken
/worker/src/match/              Forge  Halo     # the sole placer of highlights — ADR-0002
/aligner/                       Forge  Queue    # Python sidecar: transcription + match; container sizing


# ── Data, schema, and access control ─────────────────────────────────────────
